k for every unique\n17: specialization.\n18: \n19: The gate does not execute the generated kernel. It cannot detect wrong math,\n20: NaN/Inf-position differences, NPU runtime failures, or bad performance.\n21: \n22: ## Full matrix\n23: \n24: ```bash\n25: python3 integrations/cannbench/workers/run_local_matrix.py \\\n26:   --candidate-root <directory-containing-nine-modules> \\\n27:   --output-dir <evidence-directory>\n28: ```\n29: \n30: Pass criteria are 9/9 operators, 180/180 host dispatches, and 180/180\n31: compile/lowering routes. A controlled host fallback may leave a rejected\n32: specialization in the report while all case routes still pass; retain that\n33: failure as evidence rather than hiding it.\n34: \n35: ## Numerical and remote gates\n36: \n37: - Camodel: compare outputs against each task's `golden.py`, preserving its\n38:   dtype, tolerance, special-value, shape, and list-output rules. Mark large or\n39:   infeasible cases compile-only, not numerically passed.\n40: - CANNBench: the only authoritative source for real-NPU correctness and\n41:   profiler speed. Remote evaluation is opt-in and consumes a credit.\n42: \n43: For a representative smoke on this AArch64 host, build the vendored exact-v2\n44: source with `LLVM_INSTALL_PREFIX=/home/aloschilov/workspace/llvm`. The CMake\n45: graph has an observed generated-header race: if a parallel clean build misses\n46: `AscendCDialect.h.inc`, run once with `PYASC_SETUP_JOBS=1`, then continue the\n47: same build directory in parallel. GCC `-O3` may use roughly 12 GB RSS and about\n48: 15 minutes for `Translation.cpp`.\n49: \n50: After installing the resulting native wheel into an isolated Python 3.10\n51: environment with torch, run:\n52: \n53: ```bash\n54: python3.10 integrations/cannbench/workers/run_camodel_smoke.py \\\n55:   --candidate-root <generated-bundle>/cann_bench \\\n56:   --output <evidence.json>\n57: ```\n58: \n59: Use `--suite critical` for selected dtype/control-flow branches and split\n60: `--ops` into short groups when the simulator's process time budget is limited.\n61: Use `--suite adversarial --ops gelu,foreach_addcdiv_scalar` before promoting\n62: either of those operators: it covers both GELU modes, wide negative ranges,\n63: BF16, runtime scalars, and NaN/Inf positions with task-derived tolerances.\n64: Inspect simulator diagnostics as well as output comparisons: padded lanes may\n65: execute invalid arithmetic even though `real_shape` prevents them being stored.\n66: \n67: This smoke is `verified-camodel-smoke`, not `verified-camodel`, unless its\n68: declared routes cover the complete benchmark task.\n\n(End of file - total 68 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Local validation ladder\n\n## Exact-v2 compile gate\n\nRun from the repository root:\n\n```bash\nintegrations/cannbench/workers/run_local_compile_gate.sh \\\n  --candidate path/inside/repository/candidate.py --op <operator>\n```\n\nThe Docker/QEMU gate installs the self-contained CPython 3.12 x86_64 wheel\nbuilt from `compiler-team/pyasc` branch `v2`, commit\n`ac1222a48c8914d3f81297c7570d1a84f0f26778`. It replays all 20 case shapes,\ndtypes, and attrs, captures host-selected JIT launches, and runs codegen,\ncompiler passes, AscendC translation, and the 950PR UB check for every unique\nspecialization.\n\nThe gate does not execute the generated kernel. It cannot detect wrong math,\nNaN/Inf-position differences, NPU runtime failures, or bad performance.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-cannbench-kernel/references/local-validation.md","text":"# Local validation ladder\n\n## Exact-v2 compile gate\n\nRun from the repository root:\n\n```bash\nintegrations/cannbench/workers/run_local_compile_gate.sh \\\n  --candidate path/inside/repository/candidate.py --op <operator>\n```\n\nThe Docker/QEMU gate installs the self-contained CPython 3.12 x86_64 wheel\nbuilt from `compiler-team/pyasc` branch `v2`, commit\n`ac1222a48c8914d3f81297c7570d1a84f0f26778`. It replays all 20 case shapes,\ndtypes, and attrs, captures host-selected JIT launches, and runs codegen,\ncompiler passes, AscendC translation, and the 950PR UB check for every unique\nspecialization.\n\nThe gate does not execute the generated kernel. It cannot detect wrong math,\nNaN/Inf-position differences, NPU runtime failures, or bad performance.\n\n## Full matrix\n\n```bash\npython3 integrations/cannbench/workers/run_local_matrix.py \\\n  --candidate-root <directory-containing-nine-modules> \\\n  --output-dir <evidence-directory>\n```\n\nPass criteria are 9/9 operators, 180/180 host dispatches, and 180/180\ncompile/lowering routes. A controlled host fallback may leave a rejected\nspecialization in the report while all case routes still pass; retain that\nfailure as evidence rather than hiding it.\n\n## Numerical and remote gates\n\n- Camodel: compare outputs against each task's `golden.py`, preserving its\n  dtype, tolerance, special-value, shape, and list-output rules. Mark large or\n  infeasible cases compile-only, not numerically passed.\n- CANNBench: the only authoritative source for real-NPU correctness and\n  profiler speed. Remote evaluation is opt-in and consumes a credit.\n\nFor a representative smoke on this AArch64 host, build the vendored exact-v2\nsource with `LLVM_INSTALL_PREFIX=/home/aloschilov/workspace/llvm`. The CMake\ngraph has an observed generated-header race: if a parallel clean build misses\n`AscendCDialect.h.inc`, run once with `PYASC_SETUP_JOBS=1`, then continue the\nsame build directory in parallel. GCC `-O3` may use roughly 12 GB RSS and about\n15 minutes for `Translation.cpp`.\n\nAfter installing the resulting native wheel into an isolated Python 3.10\nenvironment with torch, run:\n\n```bash\npython3.10 integrations/cannbench/workers/run_camodel_smoke.py \\\n  --candidate-root <generated-bundle>/cann_bench \\\n  --output <evidence.json>\n```\n\nUse `--suite critical` for selected dtype/control-flow branches and split\n`--ops` into short groups when the simulator's process time budget is limited.\nUse `--suite adversarial --ops gelu,foreach_addcdiv_scalar` before promoting\neither of those operators: it covers both GELU modes, wide negative ranges,\nBF16, runtime scalars, and NaN/Inf positions with task-derived tolerances.\nInspect simulator diagnostics as well as output comparisons: padded lanes may\nexecute invalid arithmetic even though `real_shape` prevents them being stored.\n\nThis smoke is `verified-camodel-smoke`, not `verified-camodel`, unless its\ndeclared routes cover the complete benchmark task.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":68,"totalLines":68,"truncated":false}},"title":"skills/pyasc-cannbench-kernel/references/local-validation.md","time":{"start":1788373463019,"end":1788373463025}},"id":"prt_0635d6eae001aglZUnkIzd8gNb","sessionID":"ses_f9ca71b91ffewQRTriYo8hGE0r","messageID":"msg_0635931c9001DWsYH9FMOj9BO8"}}
